WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.567
Tier two.

2
00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:04.111
These skills are the pay multipliers.

3
00:00:04.111 --> 00:00:07.933
Each one reportedly adds to your offer, because supply is thin.

4
00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.400
Here is the good news.

5
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.567
You do not need every one of these.

6
00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:14.800
Two done deeply beats six mentioned.

7
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.200
Here are the seven, with the reported impact on an offer.

8
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.044
Agentic and multi-agent systems lead, at fifteen to twenty percent.

9
00:00:24.044 --> 00:00:27.367
Most candidates have demos, not deployed systems.

10
00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.465
MCP adds fifteen percent.

11
00:00:29.465 --> 00:00:33.567
It's a new standard with high demand and very low supply.

12
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:38.799
Fine-tuning and inference optimization each add ten to fifteen percent.

13
00:00:38.799 --> 00:00:42.133
Inference work saves lakhs a month in GPU spend.

14
00:00:42.433 --> 00:00:47.433
Hybrid search, document parsing and AI safety add about ten percent each.

15
00:00:48.633 --> 00:00:50.810
Why do these skills command a premium?

16
00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.700
Because each one is hard to find.

17
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.467
Most agent candidates only have demos.

18
00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:59.167
Inference work has measurable return, saving lakhs a month.

19
00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:05.067
Document parsing is genuinely hard, and legal, fintech and compliance teams demand it.

20
00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:10.200
And regulated industries pay for people who speak safety and guardrails fluently.

21
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.933
So what does depth look like?

22
00:01:13.233 --> 00:01:16.667
Not a demo of agents, but a system running in production.

23
00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:21.467
Not MCP on a resume line, but a server over a real database.

24
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:26.142
And hybrid search, because pure vector systems fail on IDs and names.

25
00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:27.600
Pick two and ship them.

26
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.478
If you want the quickest win, look at MCP.

27
00:01:31.478 --> 00:01:35.367
Plus fifteen percent, the fastest differentiator you can add.

28
00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:37.308
Let's recap.

29
00:01:37.308 --> 00:01:40.767
Each of these skills adds roughly ten to twenty percent.

30
00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.633
The reason is thin supply.

31
00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:44.867
Two done deeply beats six mentioned.

32
00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:47.791
And MCP is the fastest differentiator.

33
00:01:47.791 --> 00:01:51.867
Next up: Tier three, what gets you hired over fifty others.
